  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR Englis_English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"\\\\\nIn recent years, the concept of sustainable development has gained significant attention worldwide. It encompasses not only economic growth but also social and environmental impact. The United Nations' Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) aim to address these interconnected issues by setting ambitious targets for 2030. One of the key challenges facing developing countries is accessing funding and technology necessary for sustainable practices. However, innovative solutions such as crowdfunding platforms and renewable energy projects are beginning to make a difference.\\\\\nThere is growing consensus that sustainability cannot be achieved without the collaboration of governments, businesses, and individuals alike. As such, education plays a crucial role in raising awareness and fostering a sustainable mindset among citizens.\\\\\nThe author of this article believes that while the path to sustainability is fraught with challenges, it is also filled with opportunities for positive change.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main focus of sustainable development?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Economic growth only\",\n        \"Social and environmental impact only\",\n        \"Sustainable development goals alone\",\n        \"All of the above\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"All of the above\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"Which group is particularly challenged in adopting sustainable practices?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Developed countries\",\n        \"Governments\",\n        \"Businesses\",\n        \"Developing countries\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"Developing countries\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What role does education play in sustainable development?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It is unnecessary for achieving sustainability\",\n        \"It raises awareness and fosters a sustainable mindset\",\n        \"It primarily focuses on technological advancements\",\n        \"It is only relevant for developed countries\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"It raises awareness and fosters a sustainable mindset\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as an innovative solution to sustainable development?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Crowdfunding platforms\",\n        \"Renewable energy projects\",\n        \"Government subsidies\",\n        \"International cooperation\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"Government subsidies\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards sustainable development?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Optimistic\",\n        \"Neutral\",\n        \"Perplexed\",\n        \"Disapproving\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"Optimistic\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
